   "text": "This is Fmoc-Glu(OtBu)-OH, the N-Fmoc-protected L-glutamic acid with a tert-butyl ester on the side chain.\n\n**Reading the drawing**\n- The central carbon carries an HO2C group (drawn on a hashed bond), an NH\u2013Fmoc group, and a CH2CH2 chain.\n- The chain ends in CO2tBu, so it is CH2\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)O\u2013C(CH3)3.\n- Fmoc is expanded as the fluorenylmethoxycarbonyl group, NC(=O)OCC1c2ccccc2-c2ccccc12.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- The CIP priorities at the stereocentre are N > CO2H > CH2 > H.\n- The CO2H is hashed (pointing away), so the implicit H points toward the viewer.\n- Going N \u2192 CO2H \u2192 CH2 appears clockwise in the drawing. With H toward the viewer, the true sense is reversed, so the centre is S, which is the L configuration.\n- Writing the SMILES in the order CO2H, H, N, chain gives `@@`.\n\nSMILES: O=C(O)[C@@H](NC(=O)OCC1c2ccccc2-c2ccccc12)CCC(=O)OC(C)(C)C"
